Chapter: GiconVectorTest
  cites Works chapter GopIcon
  cites Works chapter GopDraw
  cites UI chapter Vector
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 The desk's icons are eight-pixel masks shown at three or four times size.
 `gicon-render` rasterizes a PATH instead, at whatever size the surface asks
 for, into a byte of coverage per pixel.

 Three shapes, chosen so each one can fail differently. The document is
 straight segments only, so it isolates the store and the addressing from the
 flattener. The disc is `vec-circle`, which is line segments about a centre,
 so it isolates the shape constructor. The drop is TWO CUBICS and nothing
 else, so its area is the whole of what the curve arm contributes: if
 `PcBezierTo` were dropped again the path would enclose nothing and the area
 would be zero, which is the same control the vector arm uses one level down.

 Inside, outside, and a partial byte are asserted separately because only the
 third distinguishes coverage from a stencil.

Section: Body

  gvt-n : Integer = 32

  gvt-partials : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  gvt-partials (blob) (n) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= n * n then acc
    else let v = peek-byte blob i
    in let p = if v > 0 then (if v < 255 then 1 else 0) else 0
    in gvt-partials blob n (i + 1) (acc + p)

  gvt-area : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  gvt-area (blob) (n) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= n * n then acc / 255
    else gvt-area blob n (i + 1) (acc + peek-byte blob i)

  gvt-row : Text, VecPath -> Text
  gvt-row (name) (p) =
    let blob = gicon-render p gvt-n
    in name & " in=" & show (gicon-cov-at blob gvt-n 16 16)
       & " out=" & show (gicon-cov-at blob gvt-n 0 0)
       & " partial=" & show (gvt-partials blob gvt-n 0 0)
       & " area=" & show (gvt-area blob gvt-n 0 0)

Section: The Shipped Set

 Nineteen drawings reach the desk's chrome and its launcher, and eyeballing
 them one at a time on the glass does not scale and does not last. A census
 does both. Two things it catches that a picture does not make obvious: a
 contour wound so the fill INVERTS, which shows as an area near the whole
 1,024 cell box, and a shape that dropped out entirely, which shows as zero.

 Overlapping contours cancel under the even-odd rule the fill uses, so a
 drawing built from overlapping pieces loses the overlap. That failure lands
 in the middle of the range rather than at either end, so the census records
 each area rather than asserting a band: a number that moves is the signal.

  gvt-set : Integer, Text -> Text
  gvt-set (i) (acc) =
    if i >= gicon-drawn-count then acc
    else let name = gicon-drawn-name i
    in let blob = gicon-render (gicon-vec-named name) gvt-n
    in gvt-set (i + 1) (acc & name & "=" & show (gvt-area blob gvt-n 0 0) & " ")

  gvt-empty : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  gvt-empty (i) (acc) =
    if i >= gicon-drawn-count then acc
    else let a = gvt-area (gicon-render (gicon-vec-named (gicon-drawn-name i)) gvt-n) gvt-n 0 0
    in let bad = if a <= 0 then 1 else if a >= gvt-n * gvt-n then 1 else 0
    in gvt-empty (i + 1) (acc + bad)

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (gvt-row "doc " gicon-vec-doc)
    print-line-uni (gvt-row "disc" gicon-vec-disc)
    print-line-uni (gvt-row "drop" gicon-vec-drop)
    print-line-uni ("set " & gvt-set 0 "")
    print-line-uni ("empty or full : " & show (gvt-empty 0 0) & " of " & show gicon-drawn-count)
  end

